Session.md\",\"content\":\"\\n# Coding Session\\n\\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"repository\\\": \\\"owner/repo\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"pull_request_number\\\": \\\"123\\\"})`\\n\\n`bm_search(note_types=[\\\"coding_session\\\"], filters={\\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex\\\", \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"<id>\\\"})`\\n\\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\",\"frontmatter\":null,\"checksum\":\"4516eea5805c53d620f88375a781e48efaf73d3ca16c94f4d5729539dcb6752e\",\"section\":null,\"start_line\":56,\"end_line\":78,\"total_lines\":78,\"has_more\":false,\"next_start_line\":null,\"next_end_line\":null}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"}},"structuredContent":{"title":"Coding Session","permalink":"main/schemas/coding-session","file_path":"schemas/Coding Session.md","content":"\n# Coding Session\n\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n\nExamples:\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.","frontmatter":null,"checksum":"4516eea5805c53d620f88375a781e48efaf73d3ca16c94f4d5729539dcb6752e","section":null,"start_line":56,"end_line":78,"total_lines":78,"has_more":false,"next_start_line":null,"next_end_line":null}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QwEQz8RVVwXhHfa7mR1bUQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
